  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Aloo gobi",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "aloo-gobi-name"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is potato and cauliflower cooked dry with spiced oil. There is no liquid added beyond what the vegetables carry; the steam trapped under the lid does the work. The aim is tender, spice-coated vegetables with some caramelised edges, not soft mush in a sauce. The key rule: do not lift the lid too often in the middle stage, or the steam escapes and the vegetables dry out before they cook through."
          }
        ]
      },
